      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can see that 91 can be factored as $91 = 7 \\cdot 13$. \n\nNow, we can use the formula for the sum of divisors of a number. If a number has a prime factorization of $p_1^{e_1} \\cdot p_2^{e_2} \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot p_n^{e_n}$, then the sum of its divisors is given by:\n\n$\\sigma(n) = (1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\ldots + p_1^{e_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\ldots + p_2^{e_2}) \\ldots (1 + p_n + p_n^2 + \\ldots + p_n^{e_n})$\n\nIn our case, $n = 91$, $p_1 = 7$, $e_1 = 1$, $p_2 = 13$, and $e_2 = 1$. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n$\\sigma(91) = (1 + 7 + 7^2)(1 + 13 + 13^2) = 57 \\cdot 201$\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is $\\boxed{11477}$.",
