      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can do this by dividing 91 by the smallest prime number, which is 2, and continuing with successive prime numbers until we can no longer divide evenly.\n\n91 ÷ 2 = 45.5 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 3 = 30.33 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 5 = 18.2 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 7 = 13 (divisible)\n\nSo, 91 = 7 × 13. Both 7 and 13 are prime numbers.\n\nNow, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors of a number with prime factorization:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + p1 + p1^2 + ... + p1^k1) × (1 + p2 + p2^2 + ... + p2^k2) × ...\n\nwhere p1 and p2 are the prime factors and k1 and k2 are their respective powers.\n\nFor 91 = 7 × 13, the sum of divisors is:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + 7) × (1 + 13) = 8 × 14 = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is \\boxed{112}.",
