      "sample_index": 5,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find all the positive divisors of 91 and then sum them up. \n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of 91. We know that 91 can be factored into 7 * 13, since both 7 and 13 are prime numbers and they multiply to give 91.\n\nNext, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors of a number. If a number has prime factors p1, p2, ..., pk, and the exponents of these primes in its prime factorization are a1, a2, ..., ak respectively, then the sum of the divisors of the number is given by:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + p1^a1 * p2^a2 * ... * pk^ak)\n\nIn this case, the prime factorization of 91 is 7^1 * 13^1, so the sum of the divisors of 91 is:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + 7^1 * 13^1)\n                 = (1 + 7 * 13)\n                 = (1 + 91)\n                 = 92\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 92.",
